      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That fog sounds exhausting—like the clarity you once had has turned into something that drains rather than guides. Reaching an edge where the trail vanishes isn't failure; it might be a sign to pause and let the fog settle on its own terms. The drop ahead isn't necessarily an end—sometimes it's just a shift in perspective you haven't seen yet. You don't have to walk forward today; resting at the edge is still part of the journey.",
